  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 104 PM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nBehind our system from Tuesday, most model agreement continues to\nsee upper-level flow shift to a more northwesterly flow over the\nPanhandles as we get trapped between two closed upper-level low\npressure systems. This flow is expected to keep us dry and chilly\nthrough Friday with highs in the 40s to low 50s and low\ntemperatures in the 20s to 30s. By Saturday, the upper-level flow\ndoes begin to shift to a more zonal flow with some hints at\ndisturbances building and pushing across the area over the\nweekend. However, current model agreement is quite messy with\nthese disturbances, with most ensembles preferring to keeping any\nchances of precipitation below 10 percent. Otherwise, this shift\nin flow does look to help warm us back up a bit with high\ntemperatures looking to return to the mid to upper 50s over the\nweekend.",
